  "candidateSpeaking": "Introduce Elena and Diego to a patient new classmate, including their origins and Elena’s music studies. Ask the classmate’s name informally, then ask the same name question formally with vous for an unfamiliar adult. Clarify that the group studies Spanish, answer a related question, and close with a suitable nice-to-meet-you phrase.",
  "candidateGrammar": {
    "explanation": "French introductions use je suis for identity, venir de or être de for origin, and s’appeler for names: je m’appelle Ana, mon camarade s’appelle Diego. Tu is informal; vous is used with an unfamiliar adult or in a formal setting. Bonjour and enchanté(e) can make a first meeting more polite.",
    "model": {
      "introduce": "Bonjour, je suis Elena.",
      "origin": "Je viens du Pérou et j’étudie la musique.",
      "classmate": "Mon camarade s’appelle Diego.",
      "formal question": "Comment vous appelez-vous ?"
    },
    "caution": "Use tu with a classmate and vous with an unfamiliar adult. Bonjour works in both settings. When asking a name, the reflexive form is Comment tu t’appelles ? or formally Comment vous appelez-vous ?"
  },
